  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations in Alabama are $12.4B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $9B, making the Department of Defense the dominant buyer by a wide margin. Award activity includes 86,449 awards and an average award size of $144K. Obligations fell 31.6% year over year. Annual context shows a fiscal progression of $13.1B in FY21, $14.1B in FY22, $14.9B in FY23, $17.3B in FY24, $18.1B in FY25, and $12.4B in FY26. Top buying agencies after the Department of Defense are the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $1.8B, the General Services Administration with $425M, and the Department of Homeland Security with $418M. Top vendors include THE BOEING COMPANY with $1.2B, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION with $1.2B, and DYNETICS, INC. with $1B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry with $3.6B in obligations, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing with $2B. The data cover contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Alabama?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $9B in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the second-largest buyer with $1.8B. Total obligations are $12.4B across 86,449 awards with an average award size of $144K. Obligations fell 31.6% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate Alabama contract obligations?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry with $3.6B in obligations. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the second-largest industry with $2B. THE BOEING COMPANY and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION each have $1.2B in obligations, and DYNETICS, INC. has $1B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Alabama?",
      "a": "Alabama received $12.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total obligations across prior fiscal years were $13.1B in FY21, $14.1B in FY22, $14.9B in FY23, $17.3B in FY24, $18.1B in FY25, and $12.4B in FY26. The state recorded 86,449 awards in FY2026 to date and an average award size of $144K. Obligations fell 31.6% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Alabama?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Alabama, obligating $9B in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the second-largest buyer with $1.8B, followed by the General Services Administration with $425M and the Department of Homeland Security with $418M. Other significant buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs with $365M and the Department of Justice with $269M."
